Begin3
Title:		Zero Point          
Version:        0.9.4
Entered-date:   11/12/98
Description:    A video game that's simple but challenging. The game presents 
		the player with a walking line like those in screensavers. The
		object of the game is to use the arrow keys to affect the 
		motion of the line. When the player stops the line, he/she 
		moves to the next level, with either a faster line, or a 
		moving polygon, depending on the level. The program was 
		written with the VGUI, so it can be compiled on either 
		Linux/X11 or Windows95.
Keywords:       Walking-line ZeroPoint video game Linux/X11 Windows95 VGUI
Author:         enumerate@rocketmail.com (Tim Farnum)
Maintained-by:  enumerate@rocketmail.com (Tim Farnum)
Primary-site:   sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/X11/games
		282KB  ZeroPoint-0.9.4.tgz
		1KB    ZeroPoint-0.9.4.lsm
Alternate-site: 
Original-site:  
Platforms:      Linux/X11 (included executable compiled on ELF with glibc6)
		VGUI needed for compiling  
		Windows95 executable included in archive.
Copying-policy:	GPL
